+### Turning Off Wiki Reads for Agents
+
+To stop agents from reading the wiki (for example to compare runs with and without wiki context), set this in `.ta/workflow.toml`:
+
+```toml
+[wiki]
+seed_context = false
+```
+
+The default is `true`, and a missing section or key also means `true`. This is a read-side switch only. With it off:
+
+- `ta_wiki_search`, `ta_wiki_get` and `ta_wiki_types` are refused by the gateway, including for chat-mode sessions. A cached page is not served either. The error names the setting and the file and says to set `seed_context = true` to turn reads back on.
+- `ta_wiki_create` and `ta_wiki_update` keep working and still go through draft review.
+- The background wiki cache sync is paused.
+- `ta doctor` shows a `Wiki reads` line explaining why reads are refused.
+
+A value that is not `true` or `false` is reported as an error that names `.ta/workflow.toml` and the `seed_context` key. Wiki reads are refused until you fix it.
+
